z3-4.3.2's Windows build returns a literal "success" instead of a real sat/unsat/unknown verdict for check-sat on this quantified problem -- not a valid SMT-LIB check-sat response, so it fails conformance review and can't be goldened. Likely the same class of extra/misplaced-success bug already documented and worked around for push() in Solver_z3_4_3_2 (see that class's comment), but manifesting for check-sat under quantifier instantiation instead; needs a real Windows z3-4.3.2 binary to diagnose further -- local testing in this project is macOS-only. See https://github.com/smtlib/jSMTLIB/issues/103.
